WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.833
GPT.

2
00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:08.300
A model trained on one deceptively simple objective, and capabilities nobody trained for appeared.

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.133
GPT is the decoder-only lineage.

4
00:00:12.433 --> 00:00:13.703
No labels, no tasks.

5
00:00:13.703 --> 00:00:17.767
Just trillions of tokens and the pressure to continue them well.

6
00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:24.200
Scale it up, and translation, code and reasoning-like behavior emerge, none of it trained directly.

7
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.633
At inference, one loop does everything.

8
00:00:27.933 --> 00:00:29.667
A forward pass runs the model.

9
00:00:29.967 --> 00:00:33.433
It gives a probability for every token in the vocabulary.

10
00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:36.233
We sample one token from that distribution.

11
00:00:36.533 --> 00:00:38.000
We append it, and repeat.

12
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.133
After flight, we see a pressure, the model might spread its odds like this.

13
00:00:43.433 --> 00:00:46.788
Drop is likely, but spike and increase still have a chance.

14
00:00:46.788 --> 00:00:48.267
Sampling picks among them.

15
00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:53.067
Temperature, top-k and top-p all act at the sample step.

16
00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:56.667
Low temperature makes the output nearly deterministic.

17
00:00:56.967 --> 00:00:59.800
High temperature makes it varied, even chaotic.

18
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.433
Here is that loop with GPT-2.

19
00:01:03.733 --> 00:01:06.933
We run the model and keep the scores for the last position.

20
00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.900
We divide by the temperature before softmax.

21
00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:13.633
We sample a token rather than always taking the top one.

22
00:01:13.933 --> 00:01:15.933
Then we append it and go around again.

23
00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:19.033
These numbers matter in production.

24
00:01:19.333 --> 00:01:23.967
A retrieval system uses temperature zero point one for factual answers.

25
00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:28.100
A research agent uses zero point seven when brainstorming.

26
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.032
Both tune the sampling step you just wrote.

27
00:01:31.032 --> 00:01:34.767
Temperature stops being folklore; it is a division on logits.

28
00:01:35.967 --> 00:01:36.857
Let's recap.

29
00:01:36.857 --> 00:01:38.933
GPT predicts the next token.

30
00:01:39.233 --> 00:01:41.233
Scale makes capabilities emerge.

31
00:01:41.533 --> 00:01:44.333
The loop is predict, sample, append, repeat.

32
00:01:44.633 --> 00:01:47.293
And temperature lives in the sample step.

33
00:01:47.293 --> 00:01:48.267
Next up: LLaMA.
